    "content": "Fátima, Portugal, is a major Catholic pilgrimage site famous for the 1917 Marian apparitions witnessed by three shepherd children—Lúcia Santos and her cousins Francisco and Jacinta Marto. The Lady of the Rosary revealed three secrets, focused on prayer, a vision of hell, and the need for devotion to her Immaculate Heart to prevent world conflicts, culminating in the \"Miracle of the Sun\" on October 13, 1917, where thousands witnessed the sun appearing to dance and fall. Key Aspects of Fátima: The Children: Lúcia Santos (10), Francisco Marto (9), and Jacinta Marto (7) were tending sheep in the Cova da Iria when they saw the apparition. The Three Secrets: Revealed to the children in July 1917, the secrets included a terrifying vision of hell, a prophecy regarding World War II, and instructions to consecrate Russia to the Immaculate Heart of Mary, with a third, long-hidden portion detailing a \"bishop in white\" navigating a damaged city of dead, interpreted as the Pope suffering in the church's struggle. Miracle of the Sun: On October 13, 1917, about 50,000 to 100,000 people witnessed the sky clear, the sun spin, emit colors, and appear to plunge toward the earth. History & Significance: Once a small village, it was named after a Moorish princess. It grew into a major Catholic center following the apparitions. Pope Pius XII designated the sanctuary as a minor basilica in 1954. Shrine of Fátima: The site includes the Chapel of the Apparitions, the Basilica of Our Lady of the Rosary, and the modern Basilica of the Most Holy Trinity. The message of Fatima focuses on praying the Rosary daily for world peace, repentance, and the conversion of sinners.",
